### TL;DR

Radiant cut and princess cut are the two square-to-rectangular brilliant shapes that compete for the same buyer. Both are modern. Both are priced 15–25% below round. The differences that matter are structural, not cosmetic.

**The Clarity Forgiveness Index:** Radiant's 70-facet crushed-ice architecture masks SI1 inclusions with a 60–70% eye-clean rate. Princess cut's chevron facets expose inclusions at only 10–30%. The same SI1 grade is a reliable buy in radiant and a risky gamble in princess.

**The Corner Tax:** Princess cut's sharp 90-degree corners chip under impact. Radiant's clipped 45-degree corners do not. Every princess ring needs corner-protecting prongs. Every chipped corner is a costly repair. That is the hidden Corner Tax of buying princess.

→ Entry princess ring: [1ct F-VS2 GIA at $2,141](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/27970851?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) + [Knife Edge Solitaire at $925](https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings/design-your-own-ring/knife-edge-solitaire-by-james-allen-item-316048?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) = **[$3,066](https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings/design-your-own-ring/knife-edge-solitaire-by-james-allen-item-316048?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational)**. Entry radiant ring: [1ct G-VS2 GIA at $2,318](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/25995245?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) + setting = **[$3,243](https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings/design-your-own-ring/knife-edge-solitaire-by-james-allen-item-316048?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational)**. Lab-grown radiant entry: [1ct E-VVS1 at $867](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/29417414?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) + setting = **[$1,792](https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings/design-your-own-ring/knife-edge-solitaire-by-james-allen-item-316048?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational)**.

