## Master Comparison: Radiant vs Princess vs Asscher

All three square brilliant or square step-cut shapes compared on every factor that matters to buyers.

| Factor | Radiant Cut | Princess Cut | Asscher Cut | What this means |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| **Cut style** | Brilliant (crushed-ice) | Brilliant (chevron X-pattern) | Step-cut (hall-of-mirrors) | Radiant and princess both sparkle; Asscher is a completely different optical product |
| **Facets** | 70 | 50–58 | 72 | More facets ≠ better sparkle — facet architecture matters more than count |
| **Corner type** | Clipped 45° — safe | Sharp 90° — chip risk | Clipped — safe | Princess corners chip under impact; radiant and Asscher corners do not |
| **Clarity floor** | SI1 (video verified) | VS2 — non-negotiable | VS1 — strict | Radiant is 1–2 grades more forgiving — real money saved at the same budget |
| **SI1 eye-clean rate** | 60–70% | 10–30% | Not applicable | SI1 in radiant is a reliable buy; SI1 in princess fails 70–90% of the time |
| **GIA cut grade** | None | Yes (Excellent/VG/Good) | None | Only princess lets you verify cut quality directly on the certificate |
| **Color floor (white metal)** | H | G (corner warmth risk at H) | G | Princess needs better color than radiant — chevron facets concentrate tint at corners |
| **Sparkle type** | High-freq shimmer, all facets | Bold X-pattern, 4 quadrants | Concentric step reflections | Radiant = constant shimmer; princess = dramatic flash; Asscher = depth and transparency |
| **L/W flexibility** | Square to elongated 1.00–1.45 | Square only 1.00–1.05 | Square only 1.00–1.05 | Only radiant can go elongated — princess and Asscher are strictly square shapes |
| **Price vs round** | −15 to −25% | −20 to −30% | −10 to −20% | Princess is cheapest vs round; Asscher offers the smallest discount |
| **Best setting** | 4-prong square or bezel | 4-prong corner-protecting only | 4-prong square | Princess requires corner prongs specifically — a non-negotiable setting constraint |
| **Fire (colored light)** | Distributed, all facets | Concentrated in 4 zones | Low — step-cuts absorb | Asscher kills fire; radiant spreads it evenly; princess fires it in 4 directed zones |

**Verdict:** Radiant wins 9 of 12 factors for everyday wear — corner safety, clarity flexibility, color tolerance, setting options, and L/W range. Princess wins on one factor that matters: GIA grades its cut, so you can verify quality on the certificate without reading proportion data manually. Asscher is not competing with either — it is a different product with different use cases.

**The Asscher position.** Asscher cut is a step-cut shape — hall-of-mirrors concentric reflections, not brilliant fire. It requires VS1 minimum clarity because step facets expose inclusions that brilliant facets would mask. It is positioned above emerald cut in the step-cut family due to its square outline, not because it produces more brilliance. Buyers who want square diamonds with fire should choose princess or radiant — Asscher delivers a completely different visual character.

